<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE hi2txt SYSTEM "hi2txt.dtd">
<hi2txt>
  <!--
    wbmlvcd  (Wonder Boy in Monster Land, Sega System 2, 1987 - decrypted
    bootleg of the Vics licensed set; clone of wbml).

    The game keeps NO native high-score file (no nvram / eeprom) and shipped
    with no hiscore.dat entry for this clone. It only ever displays a single
    "HIGH" value on screen; there is no name/initials table.

    wbmlvcd shares wbml's :maincpu work-RAM map exactly (verified by dumping a
    save state: gate bytes c101=0x24, 072f=0x03 and the default HIGH byte
    c17d=0x03 all match wbml's hiscore.dat entry byte-for-byte). A hiscore.dat
    entry for wbmlvcd was added to the shared wbml block so the MAME hiscore
    plugin now persists the score and writes a 10-byte .hi.

    The .hi is the plugin's concatenation of the 10 one-byte blocks, in DAT
    order:
      +0 c101  gate 0x24
      +1 072f  gate 0x03
      +2 c179  00
      +3 c17a  00
      +4 c17b  00
      +5 c17c  00
      +6 c17d  HIGH score, byte 1  (packed BCD, big-endian)
      +7 c17e  HIGH score, byte 2
      +8 c17f  HIGH score, byte 3
      +9 c180  00
    So the HIGH score is a 3-byte big-endian packed-BCD field at offset 6.
    Default = 03 00 00 = 30000 (matches snap 0001). Proven live: forcing
    c17e=0x45 produced .hi "...03 45 00..." and the plugin saved it, i.e.
    HIGH = 034500. base="16" reads the packed 2-digits-per-byte BCD
    (decoding-profile="bcd" would be unpacked and wrong).
    Authored by the HI2TXT project (wbmlvcd support).
  //-->

  <structure file=".hi">
    <check>
      <size>10</size>
    </check>
    <elt size="2" type="raw" id="GATE"/>
    <elt size="4" type="raw" id="PAD"/>
    <elt size="3" type="int" id="HIGH" base="16"/>
    <elt size="1" type="raw" id="TAIL"/>
  </structure>

  <output>
    <table id="HIGH SCORE">
      <column id="HIGH SCORE" src="HIGH"/>
      <column id="GATE" format="0x" display="debug"/>
      <column id="PAD"  format="0x" display="debug"/>
      <column id="TAIL" format="0x" display="debug"/>
    </table>
  </output>
</hi2txt>
